From 07f90549e917539df83d493e56b01d23c9003259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "billding.df" <billding.df@alibaba-inc.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:01:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(build): add CUDA-compatible SAIL platform support

Re-add SAIL as a CUDA-compatible in-tree platform, following the
upstream PPU platform pattern (reference commit 8f8c2968cf13):

- SRTPlatform.get_jit_cuda_arch_suffix() JIT compilation hook with a
  safe "" default for all platforms
- SailSRTPlatform overrides the hook: 810/810e devices (ZW tag in the
  device name) require the "sm80a" arch variant for JIT compilation
- JIT arch detection consults current_platform on SAIL instead of the
  removed capability-based _sail_arch_suffix helper
- Unit tests for SAIL platform identity, capabilities and the
  arch-suffix hook

The platform detection layer (PlatformEnum.SAIL, is_sail(),
is_sail_runtime(), SailSRTPlatform discovery fallback) was preserved
through the revert and is reused as-is.
