From 890b32c666ca22768fbf79ed39f5d9ecad45b8bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "billding.df" <billding.df@alibaba-inc.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:42:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(build): add nvcc-based setup_sail.py for
 CUDA-compatible SAIL kernel build

Provide a working sgl-kernel source build for the SAIL/PPU platform now
that the hgcc/sailify stack is gone. On a SAIL host nvcc is the PPU SDK's
CUDA-compatible driver (reads .cu directly, accepts -gencode, and the SDK
ships real libcudart/libcublas/libcublasLt/libcuda), so the kernel builds
through the standard torch CUDAExtension path -- no source translation.

- setup_sail.py: CUDAExtension + nvcc, gencode pinned to sm_80 (ZW810E is
  capability 8.0), real CUDA libs (c10/cuda/cublas/cublasLt), third-party
  actlize/flashinfer/triton clone, sources relativized to satisfy
  setuptools assert_relative. No torch pin in setup() deps.
- common_extension_sail.cc: SM80 op surface only; the SM90+/CUTLASS ops
  (fp8/int8 scaled_mm, cutlass_w4a8_moe, es_sm100_*, dsv4_fused_*,
  infllm_v2_*) are trimmed -- they don't target ZW810E and are served by
  PPU-native backends. Trimmed op wrappers resolve torch.ops lazily, so
  import sgl_kernel stays valid.

Verified in the fengding_step5 container: common_ops.so builds, imports,
rmsnorm is registered, and torch stays 2.13.0+ppu2.2.0.
